  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -2,
  "section_notes": "S2 keeps the 5% limit and bars public per-model publication, but sales never have to stop: the regulator may restrict sales, so a model above 5% such as Hearth 10 (6.2%) can keep selling during corrective action. S5 imposes a mandatory recall at 8 per 100,000 with no transition or interim trigger, which directly reaches Ember 8 (9.9); S3 gives new units 24 months and retrofits 72 months, which is weaker than the 12-month new-unit benchmark. S1 is the strongest section, with 24-hour reporting of all thermal incidents that applies to both companies' unreported incidents."
